    "overviewMarkdown": "# Pixie Lore\n\nPixies are among the **oldest manifested fae** known to exist, born not of flesh but of **Avalon\u2019s will and magic**. They are living expressions of elemental harmony, curiosity, and the unstable boundary between realms.\n\nThough small in stature, pixies have left **outsized marks on history**, often unnoticed by mortals until centuries later.\n\n---\n\n## Origins of the Pixie\n\nPixies first emerged during the **Early Bloom of Avalon**, when the Fae Realm stabilised after its initial formation. Unlike other fae who formed courts or hierarchies, pixies manifested as **free-roaming spirits**, each bound to a single elemental truth.\n\nPixies were never meant to rule, conquer, or guide.  \nThey were created to **observe, influence, and subtly correct** the flow of magic between realms.\n\nFrom their first moments, pixies were incomplete.\n\nEach pixie was born with **half a soul**, the other half forming separately as a **Sprite**. Together they form a complete metaphysical whole, though separated by form and purpose.\n\n---\n\n## The Split Soul Doctrine\n\nPixie lore teaches that a soul divided can better perceive reality.\n\n- Pixies experience the **active world** \u2014 emotion, action, impulse\n- Sprites experience the **reflective world** \u2014 memory, intuition, balance\n\nAncient pixies believe this division prevents corruption, arrogance, and stagnation. A whole soul, they claim, grows rigid. A split soul remains adaptable.\n\nThis belief has never been universally accepted among the fae.\n\n---\n\n## The Worldroot Gate (Tree Portal)\n\nPixies do not freely cross between realms.\n\nInstead, they rely on a living construct known as the **Worldroot Gate** \u2014 an immense, ancient tree whose roots exist simultaneously in **Avalon** and **Asteria**.\n\n### Key Facts\n- The gate opens **once every 50 years**\n- It remains open for **a single full lunar cycle**\n- Only pixies, sprites, and bonded fae may pass freely\n- Mortals who attempt passage rarely survive unchanged\n\nTo pixies, this event is known as **The Crossing Bloom**.\n\n---\n\n## The Crossing Bloom\n\nThe Crossing Bloom is a time of:\n- Celebration\n- Mourning\n- Oaths\n- Long journeys\n\nPixies born in Avalon may choose to:\n- Visit Asteria\n- Remain behind permanently\n- Escort bonded sprites or fae envoys\n- Observe the state of magic in the mortal realm\n\nPixies who pass through often do not return for centuries \u2014 if at all.\n\nThose who miss the Crossing Bloom must wait **another 50 years**, a delay that can feel unbearable to beings defined by curiosity.\n\n---\n\n## Pixies in Asterian History\n\nPixies rarely appear in written mortal records, but their influence is undeniable.\n\nThey prefer to act as:\n- Whispered guides\n- Unseen helpers\n- Saboteurs of great evils\n- Inspirers of invention and art\n\nMany pivotal moments in Asterian history coincide with **Crossing Bloom years**, though few mortals recognise the pattern.\n\n---\n\n## Notable Pixie Figures\n\n### \u2726 Queen Lythiriel of the Shimmergrove\nThe only pixie ever acknowledged as a **queen**.\n\nLythiriel united scattered pixie enclaves during a time when the Worldroot Gate was damaged by planar instability. Her reign lasted only one Crossing Bloom, after which she dissolved her crown and vanished into Avalon\u2019s upper canopies.\n\nPixies still swear rare oaths **\u201cby Lythiriel\u2019s Leaves.\u201d**\n\n---\n\n### \u2726 King Bramblethorn (The Unwilling King)\nA title bestowed by mortals, not pixies.\n\nBramblethorn led a resistance against a demonic incursion that attempted to corrupt the Worldroot Gate during a Crossing Bloom. Though victorious, he rejected all authority afterward and shattered his staff into seeds scattered across Asteria.\n\nSome believe those seeds still grow into **warded trees**.\n\n---\n\n### \u2726 Nyx-of-the-Falling-Ash\nA pixie hero bound to fire.\n\nNyx is credited with:\n- Diverting a volcanic eruption\n- Burning a lich\u2019s phylactery without destroying the soul cycle\n- Teaching early fire-mages restraint\n\nNyx never returned to Avalon and is believed to have **faded into pure flame**.\n\n---\n\n## Pixie Artisans & Crafters\n\nPixies rarely craft physical goods, but when they do, their work is legendary.\n\n### \u2726 The Glimmerhands\nA collective of pixie artisans known for crafting:\n- Ever-burning lanterns\n- Floating instruments\n- Soul-safe crystal foci\n\nEach item crafted by a Glimmerhand is said to contain a **single truthful memory** of its maker.\n\n---\n\n### \u2726 Thistlewick the Binder\nAn eccentric pixie who specialised in **binding magic to form**.\n\nThistlewick helped design early enchantment frameworks still used by Asterian artificers today. Many do not realise the \u201codd inefficiencies\u201d in these designs were intentional safety limits.\n\n---\n\n## Pixies & Mortals\n\nPixies regard mortals with fascination and caution.\n\nThey admire:\n- Creativity\n- Defiance\n- Emotional depth\n\nThey fear:\n- Obsession\n- Exploitation of magic\n- Attempts to control the Worldroot Gate\n\nPixies may aid mortals they find interesting, but will abandon those who attempt to command or bind them.\n\n---\n\n## Modern Pixie Beliefs\n\nIn the current age, pixies believe:\n- The realms are drifting further apart\n- Crossing Blooms feel more dangerous\n- Magic in Asteria is becoming volatile\n\nSome whisper that the Worldroot Gate may **one day fail entirely**.\n\nIf that happens, pixies will be forced to choose:\n- Remain forever in Avalon  \n- Or become permanent residents of the mortal realm\n\n---\n\n## Final Words of Pixie Lore\n\n> *\u201cWe are not small because we are weak.  We are small so the world forgets to fear us.\u201d*  \n> \u2014 Old Pixie Proverb\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 Notes\n\n- Native to **Avalon (Fae Realm)**  \n- Do not form structured societies  \n\nCommon habitats:\n- Elemental groves  \n- Floating crystal formations  \n- Hidden fae sanctuaries  \n\nValues:\n- Freedom  \n- Expression  \n- Balance with nature  \n- Soul connection",
