    "overviewMarkdown": "### Population\n\n**Current Population:** 10,000\u201312,000\n\nThe Polaris Ursa are considered a declining race. Though still respected throughout the frozen regions of Asteria, their numbers have never fully recovered from the devastation of the Great War approximately 1,000 years ago.\n\nBefore the war, the Polaris Ursa population was estimated between **30,000 and 35,000 individuals**, spread across numerous clans, settlements, and noble families throughout the southern polar regions of Altarin.\n\nThe war resulted in:\n\n- The destruction of dozens of clans\n- The loss of countless settlements\n- The extinction of many noble bloodlines\n- The near-collapse of Polaris Ursa civilization\n\nToday every Polaris Ursa birth is celebrated as a blessing from Nevara and a sign that their people continue to endure.\n\n---\n\n### Homeland\n\n**Original Homeland:** Altarin\n\n**Secondary Homeland:** Noran\n\nAll Polaris Ursa were originally born and raised within the frozen southern continent of **Altarin**, where they lived alongside the Ice Elves for thousands of years.\n\nFollowing the Great War, the surviving leaders feared that keeping their remaining population concentrated within a single continent could eventually lead to their extinction.\n\nTo preserve the future of their people, the surviving clans divided their population between two continents.\n\nToday the Polaris Ursa maintain homes in both Altarin and Noran.\n\n---\n\n### The Four Great Clans\n\nOnly four major clans survived the Great War.\n\nThese clans became the foundation upon which modern Polaris Ursa civilization was rebuilt.\n\n#### Frostclaw Clan\n**Ruling Family:** House Frostbjorn\n\nKnown for:\n- Leadership\n- Nobility\n- Military command\n- Diplomacy\n\nThe Frostclaw Clan is considered the oldest and most politically influential of the surviving clans.\n\n---\n\n#### Glacierheart Clan\n**Ruling Family:** House Ishald\n\nKnown for:\n- Priests\n- Shamans\n- Lorekeepers\n- Runecrafters\n\nThe Glacierheart Clan preserves much of the race's surviving history, traditions, and religious teachings.\n\n---\n\n#### Snowshadow Clan\n**Ruling Family:** House Skjoldr\n\nKnown for:\n- Hunters\n- Rangers\n- Scouts\n- Explorers\n\nThe Snowshadow Clan serves as the eyes and ears of the Polaris Ursa people.\n\n---\n\n#### Stormmaw Clan\n**Ruling Family:** House Hrimvald\n\nKnown for:\n- Warriors\n- Sailors\n- Frontier defenders\n- Monster hunters\n\nThe Stormmaw Clan led much of the migration to Noran and remains renowned for its courage and martial traditions.\n\n---\n\n### Clan Distribution\n\n#### Altarin Clans\n\n- Frostclaw Clan\n- Glacierheart Clan\n\n#### Noran Clans\n\n- Snowshadow Clan\n- Stormmaw Clan\n\n---\n\n### Creation Myth\n\nAccording to Polaris Ursa tradition, the **Ice Elves were the first children of Nevara**, Goddess of Winter.\n\nThe Ice Elves were gifted beauty, wisdom, magic, and longevity.\n\nYet Nevara soon realized that her first children lacked the physical strength necessary to defend the frozen world she had created.\n\nFrom the heart of a glacier, the breath of a blizzard, and the spirit of the polar winds, she forged her second children:\n\n**The Polaris Ursa.**\n\nWhere the Ice Elves were graceful, the Polaris Ursa were mighty.\n\nWhere the Ice Elves were scholars, the Polaris Ursa were guardians.\n\nWhere the Ice Elves preserved knowledge, the Polaris Ursa protected it.\n\nTogether they became the Twin Children of Winter.\n\n---\n\n### Sacred Relationship with the Ice Elves\n\nThe Polaris Ursa do not view the Ice Elves as rivals.\n\nInstead they refer to them as:\n\n> **The Firstborn of Winter**\n\nMany Ice Elves in turn refer to the Polaris Ursa as:\n\n> **The Wardens of Winter**\n\nFor thousands of years the two races lived side by side throughout the frozen regions of Altarin, forming one of the oldest alliances in Asterian history.\n\n---\n\n### The Great War\n\nApproximately **1,000 years ago**, the Great War devastated the southern polar regions of Altarin.\n\nThe conflict nearly wiped out both the Ice Elves and the Polaris Ursa.\n\nEntire settlements disappeared beneath ice and snow.\n\nAncient temples were destroyed.\n\nCountless bloodlines vanished forever.\n\nBy the war's conclusion, the Polaris Ursa population had fallen from approximately **30,000\u201335,000 individuals** to fewer than **2,000 survivors**.\n\nOnly four great clans remained.\n\n---\n\n### The Divine Command\n\nFollowing the war, the surviving shamans and priests of the Aetherion Faith gathered to seek guidance.\n\nLegend states that Nevara herself appeared to them through dreams and visions.\n\nShe warned that if all her remaining children stayed together, another catastrophe could one day destroy them entirely.\n\nAt that same time, an Ice Elf Prince was preparing an expedition to the distant northern continent of Noran.\n\nNevara commanded:\n\n> *\"Let winter take root in two lands, so that neither may perish.\"*\n\nObeying her decree, the Polaris Ursa divided their remaining population.\n\n#### Remained in Altarin\n- Frostclaw Clan\n- Glacierheart Clan\n\n#### Journeyed to Noran\n- Snowshadow Clan\n- Stormmaw Clan\n\nAccompanied by the Ice Elf Prince and his followers, the northern clans crossed the seas and established new settlements upon the frozen continent of Noran.\n\n---\n\n### Modern Beliefs\n\nThe Polaris Ursa believe they have two sacred responsibilities:\n\n#### Preserve the Legacy of Altarin\nThe homeland of their ancestors and birthplace of their people.\n\n#### Protect the Future of Noran\nThe refuge granted to them by Nevara after the Great War.\n\nThis belief is reflected in one of their most famous sayings:\n\n> *\"One paw remains in the south. One paw stands in the north.\"*\n\nA proverb symbolizing the eternal bond between the Polaris Ursa of Altarin and Noran.\n\n---\n\n> *\"We endure the storm. We honor our ancestors. We protect what is sacred.\"*\n>\n> \u2014 Ancient Polaris Ursa Oath",
